\title{ofeIntegrateR: Integrate Point-Source and High-Resolution Spatial Data
in On-Farm Experiments}
\description{
Tools for integrating sparse point-source measurements (e.g. soil cores,
tissue samples, disease ratings) with dense spatial covariates (e.g.
EM38 surveys, yield maps) in on-farm experimentation (OFE) strip trials.
}
\details{
Two integration strategies are provided:

\describe{
\item{Kriged-covariate (\code{\link[=fit_integrated_kriged]{fit_integrated_kriged()}})}{Krige the sparse
point-source variable onto the trial grid with \code{\link[=krige_point_samples]{krige_point_samples()}},
then include the kriged surface as a fixed covariate in a spatial
mixed model of the dense response.}
\item{Joint bivariate model (\code{\link[=fit_integrated_joint]{fit_integrated_joint()}})}{Fit the dense
response and the point-source measurements jointly as two stacked
response layers sharing a spatial random effect, avoiding a separate
kriging step.}
}

\code{\link[=simulate_ofe_trial]{simulate_ofe_trial()}} generates synthetic test data for both strategies,
and \code{\link[=extract_fixed_effects]{extract_fixed_effects()}} provides a model-agnostic way to retrieve
fixed-effect (e.g. treatment contrast) estimates from either an \code{lm} or
an \code{asreml} fit.

Developed for Milestone 4 of the AAGI-CU-RD-OFE GRDC project
(\dQuote{Development of processes to integrate point-source data and
high-resolution data}).
}
